{
  "applicable": true,
  "kind": "rewrite",
  "rule": "neumann_bc_xmin",
  "note": "Nonzero-Neumann ghost rewrite at xmin (esd-6g4.9 / G10). Fires through the ESS rule engine via the fn/dim BC-kind matcher (ess-bps/ess-tox, G8): `_discretize_bc!` encodes the BC kind->fn and side->dim onto the synthetic `bc` node, so the neumann pattern discriminates from dirichlet and from xmax. The `where` clause binds $g = u's grid (var_has_grid) and $h = 1/N for that side's spatial dim (bind_side_spacing). Grid g1 has spatial_dims=[x], dim_sizes={x:4}, so xmin -> axis 1 -> dim x -> N=4 -> h=0.25. The flux value is carried symbolically as `g` to keep the golden free of constant-folding ambiguity (the 0.25 factor stays visible, pinning the $h binding). Ghost formula: u_ghost = index(u,1) + h*value = u[1] + 0.25*g (value = du/dn, outward normal derivative; at value=0 this reduces to zero_gradient_bc_xmin's index(u,1)). NOTE: this Layer-A rewrite UNIT pins that the declarative rule fires; the numeric INTEGRATION path (build_ode_problem) still throws E_BC_UNSUPPORTED via the imperative _apply_nonperiodic_bcs! shadow — see discretizations/finite_difference/neumann_bc/INTEGRATION_GAP.md.",
  "context": {
    "grids": {
      "g1": { "spatial_dims": ["x"], "dim_sizes": { "x": 4 } }
    },
    "variables": {
      "u": { "grid": "g1" }
    }
  },
  "expression": {
    "op": "bc",
    "fn": "neumann",
    "dim": "xmin",
    "args": ["u", "g"]
  }
}
